Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Laboratory 1",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394581250479834*^9, 3.394581255896365*^9}, 
   3.394810647542058*^9}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Basic  Graphics", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3948256925765657`*^9, 3.394825696660104*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Pen-&-ink mathematicians have traditionally found graphics so labor \
intensive that they have tended to avoid figures whenever \
possible\[Ellipsis]and, when a figure could not be avoided, to make do with a \
merely ",
 StyleBox["qualitative",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " representation of the points at issue.  Figures have tended to see service \
only as expository devices, used to illustrate what was already known, and \
seldom to be used as aids to discovery. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394825714326447*^9, 3.394825784768997*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " makes the production of accurate figures\[LongDash]of many \
types\[LongDash]so quick and easy that it should/will become your habit to \
look to the graphical aspects of problems even ",
 StyleBox["before",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " you have fully understood them. The graphical aspects of your mathematical \
work will therefore assume enlarged importance.  Graphics\[LongDash]formerly \
an expository device\[LongDash]has become an exploratory tool. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395927916020925*^9, 3.395927943492571*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
In today's lab we look to some of the most basic graph-generating procedures. \
In Lab 2 we will look to some more advanced procedures. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3948280288836946`*^9, 3.3948281308590918`*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826030790065*^9, 3.394826030895191*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Resources",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826047040318*^9, 3.394826048468292*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Your principal reference is at your fingertips. Go to ",
 StyleBox["Help > Documentation Center",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and click on ",
 StyleBox["Visualization and Graphics",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". You will be presented with a list of ten topical heads. Be content for \
now to open and consider the links made available under the first four of \
those heads:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826422335861*^9, 3.39482651627534*^9}, {
  3.394826566767467*^9, 3.39482661693922*^9}, {3.394826681715826*^9, 
  3.3948267246303377`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["Data Visualization",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Item1Paragraph",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826739780426*^9, 3.394826754105669*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["Function Visualization",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Item1Paragraph",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826757822248*^9, 3.394826771185349*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["Dynamnic Visualization",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Item1Paragraph",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394826772197405*^9, 3.394826781963876*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["Options & Styling",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Item1Paragraph",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3948267837180567`*^9, 3.394826795997217*^9}}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look around to get a sense of the richness of this resource. You might, for \
example, open ",
 StyleBox["Functional Visualization",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 StyleBox[" and click on ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["Plot",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ". You will be told how the command works, and be provided with ",
 StyleBox["example",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "s. Pay attention also to the",
 StyleBox[" tutorials",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (click on, for example, ",
 StyleBox["Basic Plotting",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "), ",
 StyleBox["related links",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["more about",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " that appear at the bottom of the page. You cannot possibly explore all the \
information placed thus at your command, but these are steps you will have \
frequent occasion to repeat while familiarizing yourself with ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and also even after you have become expert, for the small but critical \
details do tend to slip away."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394827081522657*^9, 3.3948271344585123`*^9}, {
  3.394827177794319*^9, 3.394827263701874*^9}, {3.394827331360326*^9, 
  3.39482743999163*^9}, {3.394827471184407*^9, 3.394827641642844*^9}, {
  3.395928006317787*^9, 3.395928085591332*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["It might be a good idea to ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["keep a ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 StyleBox["My Graphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 StyleBox[" notebook",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ", recording your successful accomplishments; it is likely to become your \
primary reference, a source of templates that you know from your own \
experience work. Such a notebook would acquire value especially with regard \
to the correct management of the numerous \"options\" which are the main \
source of confusion in this area."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.394827891036615*^9, 3.394827902799329*^9}, {
  3.3959281246177673`*^9, 3.395928129807901*^9}, {3.3959281721606817`*^9, 
  3.3959281878483543`*^9}, {3.3959282412392282`*^9, 3.395928266025815*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3948279432228327`*^9, 3.394827943327854*^9}}]
}, Open  ]],

